<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec rubber imports down 7.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec rubber imports down 7.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in December totalled 52,519 tonnes, down 7.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Dec 96	 Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		52,519	 52,998	56,774</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   34,482	 36,301	39,478</p>
<p> Indonesia	  12,467	 12,365	11,094</p>
<p> Malaysia	    4,210	  3,063	 5,106</p>
<p>Imports in 1996 were 713,792 tonnes, up 4.0 percent from 686,449 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
